      "writtenOn": "2023-10-07T18:36:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eRight, that will tell the lis2dw12 to enable the fifo threshold interrupt, but that line needs to be mapped to the ISH no?\n\nlis2dw12 config_interrupt function routes interrupt on FIFO watermark to INT1, on mainboard, this pin is connected to both EC gpio81 and ISH GP3\nISH:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/rex/rex-ish/interrupts.dtsi;l\u003d20\nand the gpio pin is defined as:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/rex/rex-ish/gpio.dtsi;l\u003d11\n\n```\t\tgpio_ec_accel_int_r_l: ec_accel_int_r_l {\n\t\t\tgpios \u003d \u003c\u0026gpio0 3 GPIO_INPUT\u003e;\n\t\t};\n```\nEC sensor is the same:\ninterrupt defined: https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/rex/interrupts.dtsi;l\u003d50\nGPIO: https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/rex/generated.dtsi;l\u003d45\n\nCurrently interrupt is enabled, and lid accel is declared as forced mode too. As a result,motion_sense task read fifo data every interrupt(about 80ms) and polling data every (about 75ms). This polling is redundant.\nread data upon interrupt: https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/motion_sense.c;l\u003d656\npolling data:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/motion_sense.c;l\u003d673",
